// Persistent-kernel proxy for the plasticity_thick_cylinder native run (oc-opt Phase G0).
//
// Question: can a CUDA port of the thick-cylinder time loop (624 nodes, 288
// LAW36 hex8 bricks, 4704 steps of under-integrated H8 + velocity-Verlet +
// bore pressure) beat the 1.03 s native CPU run, and at what distance from
// roofline?
//
// Design: ONE persistent kernel holds the whole time loop on-device (no
// per-step launch/transfer). Inside, the proxy mirrors the real port a
// Phase G1 would write:
//   * exact cylinder mesh topology (624 nodes, 288 bricks, deck masses),
//   * greedy 4-color element ordering (race-free scatter, __syncthreads
//     between colors),
//   * per element: current-config centroid Jacobian + gradients, uniform
//     strain increment, bulk viscosity (quadratic only, c1 = 0 like the
//     native plastic arm), LAW36 tabulated J2 return (perfectly plastic
//     250 MPa table, 80-iteration bisection), V B^T (sigma - q I) scatter,
//     Flanagan-Belytschko viscous hourglass,
//   * 88 bore-pressure CLOADs on the deck FUNCT/1 curve, all-node axial
//     pins (plane strain), velocity-Verlet kick-drift-kick at fixed dt,
//   * fixed dt = 0.8 x native mean (5880 steps to the 3 ms stop).
// Fidelity: transient bore/outer DX plus bore/outer residual SY must match
// the native run before timing is trusted; the report records it.
//
// Known deviations (all documented in the report): fixed dt (native adapts
// around the same mean), no rupture/deletion branches (off-scale on this
// card: rupture 1e20, ep peaks 6.6e-4), no secant-scale evolution (tensile
// t1/t2 off-scale, scale pinned 1), inverted-element guard erodes (never
// triggers; native eroded 0/288), no TH sampling or energy bookkeeping.
//
// Build: nvcc -O2 -arch=native -o cyl_proxy plasticity_thick_cylinder_cuda_proxy.cu
// Run:   ./cyl_proxy [nstep]     (default 5880, 0.8x-mean to the stop)

#include <cstdio>
#include <cuda_runtime.h>

#define CHECK(call)                                                           \
    do {                                                                      \
        cudaError_t err = (call);                                             \
        if (err != cudaSuccess) {                                             \
            printf("CUDA error %s:%d: %s\n", __FILE__, __LINE__,               \
                   cudaGetErrorString(err));                                  \
            return 1;                                                         \
        }                                                                     \
    } while (0)

